  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-61243\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p><strong>Method 1</strong> </p>\n<p>We plot the given points in the coordinate plane.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-61243-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-61243-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>The distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.</p>\n<p>From the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"16\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> units, so the distance equals <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"17\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-61243-e-1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-61243-e-1\"></div>\n\n\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Method 2</strong></p>\n<p>We can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"18\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D465 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns